// Twenty generics, each passed `first_of` for every later one (190 function arguments), so the
// lower bounds passed down through `first_of`'s compound upper bound `(T, T)` reach each generic
// through every earlier one, one round at a time. Each round only compares the members of a
// generic's expanded lower bounds that are new to it

fn first_of<T>(pair: (T, T)) -> T {
    pair.first
}

